[A10] **Owner disposition (2026-11-23 06:36): PR #975 is approved as is.** At 8x8/1if:
- STREAM_PORT_INPUT 0 owns one cluster on TDM32 slot 0 (the first TDM channel);
- ports 1-7 each own one documented "Unrouted S<p>" cluster;
- no input cluster is backed by the loopback lane, which stays off at 8x8.

This closes R894-1-F1 and R893-1-F1 (the backing's owner disposition).

Follow-up (separate work, not part of #975): a block-RAM loopback fed through the input mapping (a real "Loopback" input cluster whose samples a talker re-transmits), designed and measured on its own branch, replacing the flop-based lane's +2.3k LUT / +1.5k FF.
